[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Azure Infrastructure as Code: ARM Templates vs. Bicep vs. Terraform"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is the gold standard for managing cloud environments. In the Azure ecosystem, you have three primary tools for defining and deploying resources: Azure Resource Manager (ARM) JSON templates, Bicep, and HashiCorp Terraform. This tutorial compares these tools and demonstrates how to deploy a basic Azure Storage Account using each approach."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"Understanding the Tools"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"ARM Templates: The native Azure IaC mechanism written in JSON. Highly reliable and supports all Azure features on day one, but notoriously verbose and difficult to maintain."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Bicep: Microsoft's domain-specific language (DSL) for deploying Azure resources declaratively. It acts as a transparent abstraction layer over ARM, offering cleaner syntax, modularity, and automatic dependency resolution."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Terraform: An open-source, cloud-agnostic IaC tool by HashiCorp. It uses HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL) and maintains its own state file, making it ideal for multi-cloud environments."},{"order":7,"heading":"Prerequisites","type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites"},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"An active Azure Subscription."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Azure CLI installed and authenticated (run az login)."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Visual Studio Code with the Bicep and Terraform extensions installed."},{"order":11,"heading":"Approach 1: ARM Template (JSON)","type":"subheading","text":"Approach 1: ARM Template (JSON)"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Save the following code as template.json. Notice the verbosity required for parameters, variables, and resource definitions."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "parameters": {
    "storageAccountName": {
      "type": "string",
      "metadata": {
        "description": "Name of the storage account."
      }
    },
    "location": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "eastus"
    }
  },
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
      "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
      "name": "[parameters('storageAccountName')]",
      "location": "[parameters('location')]",
      "sku": {
        "name": "Standard_LRS"
      },
      "kind": "StorageV2",
      "properties": {
        "supportsHttpsTrafficOnly": true
      }
    }
  ]
}"},{"order":14,"heading":"Approach 2: Bicep (Recommended for Azure-Only)","type":"subheading","text":"Approach 2: Bicep (Recommended for Azure-Only)"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Save the following code as main.bicep. Bicep removes the JSON boilerplate, making it vastly easier to read and write."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"param storageAccountName string
param location string = 'eastus'

resource storageAccount 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = {
  name: storageAccountName
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard_LRS'
  }
  kind: 'StorageV2'
  properties: {
    supportsHttpsTrafficOnly: true
  }
}"},{"order":17,"heading":"Approach 3: Terraform (Cloud-Agnostic)","type":"subheading","text":"Approach 3: Terraform (Cloud-Agnostic)"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Save the following code as main.tf. Terraform requires provider configuration and manages state locally or remotely."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"terraform {
  required_providers {
    azurerm = {
      source  = "hashicorp/azurerm"
      version = "~> 3.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "azurerm" {
  features {}
}

resource "azurerm_resource_group" "rg" {
  name     = "rg-terraform-demo"
  location = "East US"
}

resource "azurerm_storage_account" "sa" {
  name                     = "mystorageaccountxyz123"
  resource_group_name      = azurerm_resource_group.rg.name
  location                 = azurerm_resource_group.rg.location
  account_tier             = "Standard"
  account_replication_type = "LRS"
}"},{"order":20,"heading":"Deployment Commands","type":"subheading","text":"Deployment Commands"},{"order":21,"type":"paragraph","text":"To deploy your infrastructure, use the respective command-line tools for each technology."},{"order":22,"type":"code","text":"# Deploy Bicep
az group create --name rg-bicep-demo --location eastus
az deployment group create --resource-group rg-bicep-demo --template-file main.bicep --parameters storageAccountName=mystoragebicep123

# Deploy Terraform
terraform init
terraform apply"},{"order":23,"heading":"Conclusion","type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"While ARM JSON templates remain foundational behind the scenes, Bicep provides the best native Azure experience for new projects. Terraform remains the premier choice if your organization operates across multiple clouds or requires advanced state management features."}]
